From 76815423040daf5a47b15cbb266ea5acb2780936 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:54:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Numerical type given by MFEM: configuration, parameters, MPI
 types

- the numerical type of mfem-mgis is the one of MFEM (MFEM_USE_SINGLE of its
  configuration): the configuration refuses a MGIS of another type
  (MGIS_REAL_TYPE, double for a MGIS without this variable) and AmgX with
  float, and exports MFEMMGIS_REAL_TYPE. SuiteSparse is optional (MFEM
  refuses it in single precision; the solvers using it are already
  conditional). A static assertion checks that MFEM and MGIS share the type.
- mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library generates the behaviours with this type
  (real_type option of mfront, global property MFEM_MGIS_REAL_TYPE) and
  sets <target>_REAL_TYPE.
- ParameterVariant stores the floating-point values as double, so that
  {"Tolerance", 1e-10} is valid with float; is<float> and get<float> read
  them converted, so that get<real> works with both types.
- MPI: the reductions of MeanThermodynamicForces and
  ComputeResultantForceOnBoundary use the MPI type of real instead of
  MPI_DOUBLE; Eval of the coefficients returns mfem::real_t; the reference
  coordinates of PeriodicNonLinearEvolutionProblem are initialized with the
  maximum of real.
Double unchanged: 216/216 tests on the CPU.
